{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Whatever has fins and scales.</b> I wonder: why were fish repeated? Granted, for animals it is explained in [chapter] חולין that it was repeated because of the שסועה, and for birds because of the ראה — but why were fish repeated more than locusts? This requires investigation. And furthermore I wonder: a third verse for fish — for it is written in the section שמיני, ״כל אשר אין לו סנפיר וקשקשת שקץ הוא״ — why do I need it? This requires investigation. In Tosafot on חולין:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The terms שסועה and ראה refer to specific halakhic categories discussed in tractate Chullin; left untranslated as technical terms as they stand. The phrase קרא שלישי ('a third verse') refers to the question of why a third scriptural source is needed for fish, beyond the two already given in Leviticus 11 and Deuteronomy 14."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:57.840245300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}